WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.808
Agencies run two free, read-only
assessments of their Microsoft cloud,

2
00:00:04.808 --> 00:00:08.496
and often drop one because
both seem to cover identity.

3
00:00:08.496 --> 00:00:10.325
But they answer different questions.

4
00:00:10.325 --> 00:00:15.482
ScubaGear is CISA's tool, and asks whether
the tenant meets the federal baseline.

5
00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:18.522
Microsoft's Zero Trust
Assessment asks how mature

6
00:00:18.522 --> 00:00:21.489
the environment is against
Microsoft's guidance.

7
00:00:21.489 --> 00:00:25.160
It's a community project
maintained by Microsoft employees,

8
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.617
not an official product, and
no support program covers it.

9
00:00:28.617 --> 00:00:32.272
They overlap on Entra ID
and some Defender policies.

10
00:00:32.272 --> 00:00:35.732
But only ScubaGear covers
Exchange Online, Teams,

11
00:00:35.732 --> 00:00:41.049
SharePoint and Power Platform, and 22 of
the 50 mandatory policies live there.

12
00:00:41.049 --> 00:00:44.727
Drop ScubaGear and you leave
mandatory policies unassessed,

13
00:00:44.727 --> 00:00:47.536
and stop the reporting
the directive requires.

14
00:00:47.536 --> 00:00:50.284
So run both, and reconcile
at the control level:

15
00:00:50.284 --> 00:00:55.997
the tenant setting, and the SP
800-53 control it supports.

16
00:00:55.997 --> 00:00:59.860
Next, everything beyond Microsoft 365.
